{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792483972,"nonce":"IMl6iiWD3K1Uqq24n059s2yj9Pk=","title":"TypeScript: intern frontend names and remove repeated metadata allocations","message":"The initial zyntax_ts frontend retains owned String keys for signatures, aliases, views, bindings and dependency traversal; formats native function names at each call; linearly scans stored layout vectors; and resolves field symbols into newly allocated strings for lookup. Use Zyntax's string interner for retained identity and native names, borrow source spellings where stable lexical ordering is required, cache each source spelling so repeated lookups do not acquire the global interner lock, and avoid copying complete signatures. Use canonical layout lookup without allocating a new retained key on cache hits. Keep name ownership, source evaluation order and readonly identity correct.\n\nResolve function dependencies with a worklist rather than recursion and use Oxc's existing resolved symbols without allocating a full semantic node table. Add a reproducible allocation audit using the compiler's existing CountingAllocator and record before/after counts in this issue. This is part of the day-one performance requirement for zynode; no throughput claim is implied by allocation counts.","files":null}]}